---
// Linked from the footer. The homepage tells people their code is stored
// here; this is the page that says exactly what that means.
import Shell from "../layouts/Shell.astro";
---

<Shell title="Privacy · tony" description="What tony stores, who can read it, and how to delete it.">
  <section class="sec">
    <p class="cap">[ privacy ]</p>
    <h2 class="big">What tony stores.</h2>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <p class="cap">[ on your machine ]</p>
    <p class="body">
      tony doesn't call a model. Your agent reads your code where it already is. tony
      sends nothing to a model provider.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <p class="cap">[ what gets uploaded ]</p>
    <p class="body">
      Publishing a review uploads it here. It includes the diff and the code around
      each change, so your source code is stored on this site.
    </p>
    <p class="body">
      tony also keeps your username, avatar, and account id; each review's repo name,
      range, and summary; which agent and model wrote it; and your sign-in session.
      tony never sees your password.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <p class="cap">[ protection ]</p>
    <p class="body">
      Reviews are encrypted with AES-256-GCM in a private store. Sign-in tokens are
      stored only as hashes.
    </p>
    <p class="body">
      <b>tony holds the key.</b> Anyone who can run code on this server, or a legal
      demand to tony, can read a review. Don't publish code you couldn't share with tony.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <p class="cap">[ who can read a review ]</p>
    <p class="body">Anyone signed in with the link. Treat it like a password.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <p class="cap">[ deleting ]</p>
    <p class="body">
      Reviews are deleted automatically after 30 days. You can delete one sooner, or
      delete your whole account, from <a href="/reviews">your reviews</a>. Both take
      effect immediately.
    </p>
    <p class="body">No ads, no third-party analytics, nothing sold.</p>
  </section>
</Shell>
